# CAPTURED emitter output, unmodified. Not a captured SWEEP: the endpoints were
# probed against a local stub, so the verdicts are the stub's and not any real
# service's, but every byte below is what prober/src/emit.rs's RunWriter wrote.
#
# Copied verbatim from prober/state/task-4-e2e/run-2.nq, the second run of the
# dormancy stage's end-to-end fixture, which is the first committed file
# carrying a NON-EMPTY dormancy section. That section is the point of this
# fixture: between the header's sw:emission terminator and the first chunk sit
# one group per endpoint the sweep declined to ask, closed by the
# sw:dormantCount terminator, which is written last and always, even at zero.
#
# 115 quads, one run graph (urn:sparqlwatch:run:2026-08-27T10:00:00Z), three
# endpoints of the same trio run-with-samples.nq holds, so this run can be
# loaded beside the real 16:00 sweep of the same three:
#
#   data.kkg.kadaster.nl/query   DORMANT. Declared with sw:dormancyReason
#     "operator-hold" and an sw:dormantSince, and it has NO chunk: no
#     measurement, no decline, no sw:declarationsRead, nothing. That is what
#     makes a dormant endpoint absent from the measured and the sampled set,
#     which is why sw:currentRun does not advance to this run for it and why
#     web/load_run.py needs no dormancy pointer at all.
#   ontop.certain.ai.ustp.at/sparql   measured, classes declined cost-ceiling.
#   qlever.dev/api/osm-planet         measured, classes declined cost-ceiling.
#
# All four terminators are present and in order (sw:emission, sw:dormantCount,
# two sw:completedEndpoint, sw:finalised), so this is also the file the
# Python-side truncation tests cut: the dormancy section is the one cut point
# run-prober-failed.nq cannot provide, because it predates the section.
#
# The instant is 2026-08-27T10:00:00Z, later than every other committed
# fixture's, so a test that loads this beside another one gets a store whose
# NEWEST run is the one that declared an endpoint dormant. That is the shape
# that makes test_a_run_that_declined_an_endpoint_does_not_become_its_current_run
# a real question rather than a vacuous one.
